--soft-clipping-protection","content":"8. Summing, Mono Downmix & Soft Clipping Protection","locale":"en"},"864":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-11","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#9-host-transport--bpm-sync","content":"9. Host Transport & BPM Sync","locale":"en"},"865":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-12","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#phase-locking-mechanism-ppq","content":"Phase Locking Mechanism (PPQ)","locale":"en"},"866":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-13","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#10-real-time-pitch-transposition-midi-in","content":"10. Real-Time Pitch Transposition (MIDI In)","locale":"en"},"867":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-14","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#11-multi-channel-polyphonic-output-midi-out","content":"11. Multi-Channel Polyphonic Output (MIDI Out)","locale":"en"},"868":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-15","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","content":"Each sequence inside Metulifer hosts its own dedicated audio synthesis engine encapsulated within the `Voice` class (`Source/DSP/Voice.{h,cpp}`).\nAll audio code strictly adheres to hard real-time audio constraints: **zero dynamic memory allocations**, **zero mutex locks**, and **zero blocking OS system calls**.","locale":"en"},"869":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-16","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#voice-signal-architecture","content":"The audio signal traverses the following stages sequentially:","locale":"en"},"870":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-17","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#1-antialiased-generators-vco-1--vco-2-with-polyblep","content":"Both oscillators evaluate waveforms via normalized phase accumulators running in `[0.0, 1.0[` paired with high-performance **polyBLEP (Polynomial Bandlimited Step)** antialiasing:","locale":"en"},"871":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-18","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#1-antialiased-generators-vco-1--vco-2-with-polyblep","content":"Four selectable waveshapes:","locale":"en"},"872":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-19","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#1-antialiased-generators-vco-1--vco-2-with-polyblep","content":"**Sine**: `sin(2 * pi * phase)` (pure spectral sine).","locale":"en"},"873":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-20","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#1-antialiased-generators-vco-1--vco-2-with-polyblep","content":"**Saw**: `(2 * phase - 1) - polyBlep(phase, increment)` (rich harmonics free of digital aliasing).","locale":"en"},"874":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-21","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#1-antialiased-generators-vco-1--vco-2-with-polyblep","content":"**Square**: binary pulse wave corrected by dual polyBLEP steps on rising and falling transitions (`phase` and `phase + 0.5`).","locale":"en"},"875":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-22","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#1-antialiased-generators-vco-1--vco-2-with-polyblep","content":"**Triangle**: `1 - 4 * abs(phase - 0.5)` (warm, soft acoustic character).","locale":"en"},"876":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-23","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#pitch-and-arpeggiator-tracking","content":"Fundamental frequency `f` is computed from base pitch (C3 = 130.81 Hz), octave switch (−2 to +2), and note interval:","locale":"en"},"877":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-24","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#pitch-and-arpeggiator-tracking","content":"When the **Arpeggiator** is engaged on a sequence, `advanceArp()` steps through the selected algorithmic pattern and musical scale, adding note offsets synchronously across both VCOs without altering their relative detune.","locale":"en"},"878":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-25","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#2-adsr-envelopes","content":"Each oscillator features an independent `juce::ADSR` envelope generator.","locale":"en"},"879":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-26","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#2-adsr-envelopes","content":"Attack, decay, and release curves follow natural exponential decay characteristics.","locale":"en"},"880":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-27","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#2-adsr-envelopes","content":"Temporal parameters use a logarithmic potentiometer taper (**skew factor 0.3**) providing fine resolution below 100 ms while allowing long swells up to 2 seconds.","locale":"en"},"881":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-28","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#3-vcf-filtering-state-variable-tpt","content":"Filter stages utilize `juce::dsp::StateVariableTPTFilter<float>`.\nTopology-preserving transform (TPT) ensures absolute numerical stability during high-speed cutoff modulation from LFOs:","locale":"en"},"882":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-29","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#3-vcf-filtering-state-variable-tpt","content":"**LPF (Low-Pass Filter)**: 12 dB/octave attenuation of high frequencies.","locale":"en"},"883":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-30","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#3-vcf-filtering-state-variable-tpt","content":"**HPF (High-Pass Filter)**: low-end sub cut and spectral thinning.","locale":"en"},"884":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-31","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#3-vcf-filtering-state-variable-tpt","content":"Logarithmic sweep range from 20 Hz to 20,000 Hz.","locale":"en"},"885":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-32","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#4-multi-fx-redux-bitcrusher--decimator","content":"The Redux effect degrades audio through two distinct degradation stages:","locale":"en"},"886":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-33","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#4-multi-fx-redux-bitcrusher--decimator","content":"**Downsampling (Temporal Decimation)**:\nA sample counter modulo `rate` latches and holds samples (Sample & Hold) over `N` frames (1 to 32).","locale":"en"},"887":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-34","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#4-multi-fx-redux-bitcrusher--decimator","content":"**Bit-Depth Quantization**:","locale":"en"},"888":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-35","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#4-multi-fx-redux-bitcrusher--decimator","content":"Variable resolution from 2 bits (extreme digital crunch) to 16 bits (clean pass).","locale":"en"},"889":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-36","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#4-multi-fx-redux-bitcrusher--decimator","content":"**Dry/Wet Crossfade**: phase-linear blend.","locale":"en"},"890":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-37","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#5-multi-fx-true-ping-pong-stereo-delay-with-cross-feedback","content":"Delay line buffers are pre-allocated during `prepare()` with capacity for 2.5 seconds of audio:","locale":"en"},"891":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-38","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#5-multi-fx-true-ping-pong-stereo-delay-with-cross-feedback","content":"**True Cross-Feedback Ping-Pong**:\nLeft channel echoes directly into the Right delay buffer, and Right echoes back into Left:","locale":"en"},"892":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-39","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#5-multi-fx-true-ping-pong-stereo-delay-with-cross-feedback","content":"**Soft Hyperbolic Tangent (`tanh`) Saturation**:\nNon-linear saturation in the feedback loop prevents runaway feedback exceeding 0 dBFS even at maximum feedback settings (up to 90%).","locale":"en"},"893":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-40","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#5-multi-fx-true-ping-pong-stereo-delay-with-cross-feedback","content":"**Dual Stereo Mode**: switchable independent L/L and R/R parallel delay lines.","locale":"en"},"894":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-41","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#5-multi-fx-true-ping-pong-stereo-delay-with-cross-feedback","content":"**Instant Buffer Purge**: delay memory is instantly zeroed when toggled off (`delayBuffer.clear()`), avoiding stale audio bursts upon re-engagement.","locale":"en"},"895":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-42","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#6-multi-fx-stereo-reverb--parameter-caching","content":"Built upon `juce::dsp::Reverb`, spatial processing follows the delay line:","locale":"en"},"896":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-43","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#6-multi-fx-stereo-reverb--parameter-caching","content":"**Room Mode**: short, dense early reflections suited for tight rhythm stabs.","locale":"en"},"897":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-44","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#6-multi-fx-stereo-reverb--parameter-caching","content":"**Hall Mode**: expansive, cathedral-like decay tail.","locale":"en"},"898":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-45","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#6-multi-fx-stereo-reverb--parameter-caching","content":"**Dirty Checking Optimization**: coefficients are recalculated only when reverb mode or mix changes, preventing comb-filter coefficient recomputation on every audio block.","locale":"en"},"899":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-46","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#7-voice-sleep--tail-management","content":"To guarantee minimal CPU footprint (< 5% under load and 0.0% idle) without abruptly cutting off natural reverb or delay tails:","locale":"en"},"900":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-47","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#7-voice-sleep--tail-management","content":"**Immediate Idle Bypass**:\nWhen envelopes are quiet (`!adsr1.isActive() && !adsr2.isActive()`) and delay/reverb are inactive, `Voice::renderChunk()` exits in **0 nanoseconds**.","locale":"en"},"901":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-48","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#7-voice-sleep--tail-management","content":"**Decay Tail Management**:","locale":"en"},"902":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-49","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#7-voice-sleep--tail-management","content":"Following note release, upstream synthesis is bypassed: **polyBLEP oscillators, ADSR envelopes, VCF filters, and Redux are completely skipped on silence**.","locale":"en"},"903":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-50","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#7-voice-sleep--tail-management","content":"Delay and reverb decay tails continue ringing out naturally for up to 4.0 seconds.","locale":"en"},"904":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-51","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#7-voice-sleep--tail-management","content":"**Acoustic Silence Detection**:\nWhen residual energy drops below -80 dBFS ($< 10^{-4}$), the voice is automatically put to sleep (`isVoiceActive = false`).","locale":"en"},"905":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-52","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#7-voice-sleep--tail-management","content":"**Instant Transient Wakeup**:\nAny `noteOn()` event immediately wakes the voice with zero latency.","locale":"en"},"906":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-53","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#8-summing-mono-downmix--soft-clipping-protection","content":"At the conclusion of `processBlock()`:","locale":"en"},"907":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-54","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#8-summing-mono-downmix--soft-clipping-protection","content":"**Automatic Mono Downmixing**:\nWhen instantiated on a mono DAW track, left and right channels from stereo delay and reverb are summed at 50% (`0.5f`), preserving all spatial effects without dropping the right channel.","locale":"en"},"908":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-55","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#8-summing-mono-downmix--soft-clipping-protection","content":"**Headroom Attenuation & Soft Saturation**:\nA 6 dB headroom trim combined with smooth hyperbolic tangent (`std::tanh`) saturation prevents digital hard clipping when all 6 polyphonic voices sum simultaneously:","locale":"en"},"909":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-56","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#8-summing-mono-downmix--soft-clipping-protection","content":"**Studio Peak & RMS Monitoring at 60 Hz**:\nReal-time per-channel peak and RMS measurements are stored into thread-safe atomic floats (`peakDbL/R`, `rmsDbL/R`) with peak hold to drive the UI's calibrated dBFS meter and phase-locked oscilloscope.","locale":"en"},"910":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-57","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#9-host-transport--bpm-sync","content":"DAW timeline synchronization leverages JUCE's `juce::AudioPlayHead` interface queried on every `processBlock()` call:","locale":"en"},"911":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-58","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#phase-locking-mechanism-ppq","content":"`ppqPosition` represents time in quarter notes (1.0 = 1 quarter note).","locale":"en"},"912":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-59","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#phase-locking-mechanism-ppq","content":"Since Metulifer steps are sixteenth notes (1/4 of a quarter note), the absolute total step index is:\n`stepTotal = std::floor(ppqPos * 4.0)`","locale":"en"},"913":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-60","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#phase-locking-mechanism-ppq","content":"Intra-step phase fraction aligns `sampleCounter` to the precise sample offset:\n`stepPhase = (ppqPos * 4.0) - std::floor(ppqPos * 4.0)`\n`sampleCounter = std::floor(stepPhase * stepLengthInSamples)`","locale":"en"},"914":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-61","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#phase-locking-mechanism-ppq","content":"Each sequence `i` sets its current step modulo its active loop length:\n`currentStep[i] = stepTotal % length[i]`\nThis guarantees rock-solid rhythmic alignment even after jumping to arbitrary positions or when working with odd time signatures in the host DAW.","locale":"en"},"915":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-62","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#10-real-time-pitch-transposition-midi-in","content":"Metulifer processes incoming MIDI note events arriving on the plugin's MIDI input:","locale":"en"},"916":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-63","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#10-real-time-pitch-transposition-midi-in","content":"Incoming MIDI notes apply a global pitch transposition relative to middle **C3 (MIDI note 60)**:\n`deltaSemitones = midiNoteNumber - 60`","locale":"en"},"917":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-64","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#10-real-time-pitch-transposition-midi-in","content":"This transposition offset is stored in `Voice::Params::transpose`.","locale":"en"},"918":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-65","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#10-real-time-pitch-transposition-midi-in","content":"Both oscillators update their fundamental frequency instantaneously without memory allocation:\n`f = 130.81 * std::exp2((double) octave + (double) (note + arpOffset + transpose) / 12.0)`","locale":"en"},"919":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-66","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#10-real-time-pitch-transposition-midi-in","content":"Enables real-time key changes and melodic transposition of running polyrhythms via external MIDI controllers or DAW piano-roll clips.","locale":"en"},"920":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-67","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#11-multi-channel-polyphonic-output-midi-out","content":"During every audio block, `SequencerEngine` collects active step gates into sample-accurate events `StepEvent`:","locale":"en"},"921":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-68","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#11-multi-channel-polyphonic-output-midi-out","content":"Each active step emits a sample-accurate `noteOn` message on its designated MIDI channel:\n`midiChannel = trackIndex + 1` (channels 1 to 6)","locale":"en"},"922":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-69","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#11-multi-channel-polyphonic-output-midi-out","content":"The pitch emitted reflects the track's root note combined with octave, note knob, and arpeggiator offsets.","locale":"en"},"923":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp-70","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/dsp#11-multi-channel-polyphonic-output-midi-out","content":"When playback is stopped or a track gate releases, corresponding `noteOff` and `allNotesOff` messages are dispatched to prevent stuck notes.","locale":"en"},"924":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","type":"page","content":"Overview","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Architecture","Architecture"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","locale":"en"},"925":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-0","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","content":"Processor, Editor, sequencer engine, voices and signal flow — the map of the source tree.","locale":"en"},"926":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-1","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#two-main-objects","content":"Two main objects","locale":"en"},"927":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-2","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#source-tree","content":"Source tree","locale":"en"},"928":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-3","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#audio-flow","content":"Audio flow","locale":"en"},"929":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-4","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#control-flow","content":"Control flow","locale":"en"},"930":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-5","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#three-serialised-states","content":"Three serialised states","locale":"en"},"931":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-6","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#where-to-go-next","content":"Where to go next","locale":"en"},"932":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-7","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#two-main-objects","content":"A JUCE plugin boils down to two classes, and Metulifer follows that model exactly:","locale":"en"},"933":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-8","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#two-main-objects","content":"| Class                     | Files                            | Role                                     |\n| ------------------------- | -------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `MetuliferAudioProcessor` | `Source/PluginProcessor.{h,cpp}` | state, parameters, sequencer engine, DSP |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"934":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-9","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#two-main-objects","content":"| Class                           | Files                         | Role                                |\n| ------------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `MetuliferAudioProcessorEditor` | `Source/PluginEditor.{h,cpp}` | UI, 30 Hz timer, cables, pagination |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"935":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-10","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#two-main-objects","content":"The processor **owns** the `AudioProcessorValueTreeState` (APVTS); the editor only\nattaches to it. That is what lets the state survive the window being closed.","locale":"en"},"936":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-11","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#audio-flow","content":"`processBlock()` is the real-time heart. It performs **no allocation** and never touches\nthe `ValueTree`: everything it needs is read from `std::atomic` values.","locale":"en"},"937":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-12","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#audio-flow","content":"The key step is 6: events carry a precise **sample offset**, so the block is split and\nnotes fire exactly on time — no jitter tied to the buffer size.","locale":"en"},"938":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-13","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#control-flow","content":"The UI never talks to the DSP directly:","locale":"en"},"939":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-14","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#control-flow","content":"`SliderAttachment`s keep a knob in sync with a parameter (both directions).","locale":"en"},"940":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-15","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#control-flow","content":"The audio thread reads the `std::atomic<float>` values exposed by the APVTS: lock-free.","locale":"en"},"941":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-16","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#control-flow","content":"The display and state buttons listen to parameters, so they also follow\n**host automation**.","locale":"en"},"942":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-17","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#three-serialised-states","content":"`getStateInformation()` writes a root `MetuliferState` `ValueTree` containing:","locale":"en"},"943":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-18","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#three-serialised-states","content":"| Child   | Content            | Type        |\n| ------- | ------------------ | ----------- |\n| `APVTS` | the 209 parameters | `ValueTree` |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"944":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-19","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#three-serialised-states","content":"| Child   | Content                                               | Type        |\n| ------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| `steps` | properties `p0`…`p5`, one 32-bit pattern per sequence | `ValueTree` |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"945":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-20","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#three-serialised-states","content":"| Child | Content                                       | Type        |\n| ----- | --------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| `mod` | one `cable { src, dest }` child per LFO cable | `ValueTree` |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"946":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-21","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#three-serialised-states","content":"Everything is converted to XML then to binary (`copyXmlToBinary`).","locale":"en"},"947":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-22","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#three-serialised-states","content":"Parameters are host-automatable; steps and cables must **not** be. Keeping them apart\navoids polluting the DAW automation with 192 steps and keeps `getStateInformation()`\nreadable.","locale":"en"},"948":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-23","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#where-to-go-next","content":"<Card title=\"Parameter reference\" href=\"/en/docs/architecture/parameters\" />","locale":"en"},"949":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-24","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#where-to-go-next","content":"<Card title=\"DSP chain\" href=\"/en/docs/architecture/dsp\" />","locale":"en"},"950":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-25","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#where-to-go-next","content":"<Card title=\"Sequencer and state\" href=\"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state\" />","locale":"en"},"951":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview-26","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/overview#where-to-go-next","content":"<Card title=\"UI and skinning\" href=\"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin\" />","locale":"en"},"952":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/overv