/docs/architecture/sequencer-state#6-lane-polyrhythmic-independence","content":"6-Lane Polyrhythmic Independence","locale":"en"},"1027":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state-3","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state#sub-block-event-slicing-process","content":"Sub-Block Event Slicing (`process`)","locale":"en"},"1028":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state-4","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state#plugin-state-serialization","content":"Plugin State Serialization","locale":"en"},"1029":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state-5","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state#architectural-benefits-of-tree-segregation","content":"Architectural Benefits of Tree Segregation","locale":"en"},"1030":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state-6","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state","content":"The sequencer engine (`Source/Sequencer/SequencerEngine.{h,cpp}`) drives step triggering and playhead animations.\nIt provides clock-tight synchronization while enabling complete metric independence across the 6 lanes.","locale":"en"},"1031":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state-7","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state#clock-engine-architecture","content":"The timing grid is governed by the global `tempo` parameter (BPM):","locale":"en"},"1032":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state-8","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state#clock-engine-architecture","content":"Each step corresponds to a **sixteenth note** (1/16th note division).","locale":"en"},"1033":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state-9","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state#6-lane-polyrhythmic-independence","content":"Unlike traditional synthesizers where a single master counter resets all tracks, each sequence `s` tracks its own fractional sample phase and its own loop length `L_s` between 1 and 32 steps:","locale":"en"},"1034":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state-10","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state#6-lane-polyrhythmic-independence","content":"Patterns slip and intertwine, generating evolving polyrhythms with zero sample drift.","locale":"en"},"1035":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state-11","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state#sub-block-event-slicing-process","content":"To eliminate timing jitter caused by variable audio host buffer sizes (e.g., 256, 512, or 1024 samples), the engine slices each audio buffer at exact sample boundaries:","locale":"en"},"1036":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state-12","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state#sub-block-event-slicing-process","content":"When a step boundary is crossed:","locale":"en"},"1037":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state-13","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state#sub-block-event-slicing-process","content":"A `gateOff` event releases the prior active note.","locale":"en"},"1038":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state-14","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state#sub-block-event-slicing-process","content":"If the active step is enabled in the sequence bitmask (`(mask & (1 << step)) != 0`), a `gateOn` event is queued with its exact intra-buffer sample offset.","locale":"en"},"1039":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state-15","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state#sub-block-event-slicing-process","content":"`Voice::renderSegment()` renders audio slices between successive event offsets.","locale":"en"},"1040":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state-16","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state#plugin-state-serialization","content":"Metulifer persists complete plugin state during DAW project saves or preset archiving via `getStateInformation()` and restores it via `setStateInformation()`.","locale":"en"},"1041":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state-17","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state#plugin-state-serialization","content":"State data is organized into a hierarchical `juce::ValueTree`:","locale":"en"},"1042":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state-18","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state#architectural-benefits-of-tree-segregation","content":"**Clean DAW Automation**: 192 step toggles and dynamic patch cables do not pollute DAW automation tracks.","locale":"en"},"1043":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state-19","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state#architectural-benefits-of-tree-segregation","content":"**Binary Performance**: The XML tree is serialized to compressed binary with `juce::copyXmlToBinary` for zero-overhead disk I/O.","locale":"en"},"1044":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state-20","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/sequencer-state#architectural-benefits-of-tree-segregat