/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin#2-multi-state-button-sprites-skindrawbuttonsprite","content":"Supports multi-state toggles and momentary switches with automatic state selection:","locale":"en"},"1139":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin-26","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin#2-multi-state-button-sprites-skindrawbuttonsprite","content":"**6-Frame Filmstrips**: `0: Off`, `1: Off Hover`, `2: Off Down`, `3: On`, `4: On Hover`, `5: On Down`.","locale":"en"},"1140":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin-27","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin#2-multi-state-button-sprites-skindrawbuttonsprite","content":"**4 & 2-Frame Filmstrips**: Simplified sprite animations.","locale":"en"},"1141":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin-28","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin#2-multi-state-button-sprites-skindrawbuttonsprite","content":"**Discrete Image Files**: Automatic discovery of `btn_<name>_on`, `btn_<name>_off`, `btn_<name>_down`.","locale":"en"},"1142":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin-29","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin#3-sequencer-step-buttons-skindrawstepbutton","content":"Supports unified `step_button_filmstrip` (with on, off, hover, down states) or discrete state assets `step_on`, `step_off`, `step_downbeat` (downbeat 4/4 grouping).","locale":"en"},"1143":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin-30","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin#4-octave-lever-switch-skindrawlever","content":"Renders 5-position octave lever switches (-2, -1, 0, +1, +2) via `lever_octave_filmstrip` or discrete images `lever_octave_0` through `lever_octave_4`.","locale":"en"},"1144":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin-31","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin#5-screen-glass-overlay-skindrawscreenoverlay","content":"Transparent 3D glass bezel with specular reflection highlights overlaid on top of the OLED oscilloscope and dB meter (`screen_glass_overlay.png`).","locale":"en"},"1145":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin-32","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin#performance--energy-invariants","content":"To maintain a rock-solid 60/120 Hz refresh rate with near-zero energy consumption:","locale":"en"},"1146":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin-33","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin#1-zero-disk-io--negative-caching","content":"**One-Time Directory Indexing**: On first query, all resource directories (`Resources/`, bundle `Contents/Resources`, etc.) are cataloged once in an in-memory `std::unordered_map<std::string, juce::File>`.","locale":"en"},"1147":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin-34","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin#1-zero-disk-io--negative-caching","content":"**Mandatory Negative Caching**: Missing assets are immediately cached as invalid images (`imageCache[key] = juce::Image()`). Subsequent 60 Hz queries hit memory in O(1) time with **zero `stat()` filesystem syscalls or disk latency**.","locale":"en"},"1148":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin-35","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin#2-macos-hardware-gpu-acceleration-setopaquetrue","content":"The root plugin editor is explicitly marked opaque.","locale":"en"},"1149":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin-36","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin#2-macos-hardware-gpu-acceleration-setopaquetrue","content":"Window dragging and repositioning is executed directly by the macOS WindowServer using GPU texture blitting with **zero CPU redraw calls**.","locale":"en"},"1150":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin-37","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin#3-coregraphics-clipping-optimization-setpaintingisunclipped","content":"All 192 sequencer step buttons and rows activate `setPaintingIsUnclipped(true)`, eliminating repetitive CoreGraphics clip path calculations.","locale":"en"},"1151":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin-38","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin#blender-3d-to-juce-workflow","content":"The vector engine serves as an ergonomic base. To integrate photorealistic hardware skins modeled in **Blender 3D**:","locale":"en"},"1152":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin-39","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin#blender-design-guidelines","content":"**Canvas Resolution**: 1280 × 720 px base (and 2560 × 1440 px `@2x` for Retina rendering).","locale":"en"},"1153":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin-40","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin#blender-design-guidelines","content":"**Knob Pivot Alignment**: Rotational knob axes in 3D scene cameras must match the exact pixel centers in `Source/PluginEditor.cpp`.","locale":"en"},"1154":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin-41","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture/ui-skin#blender-design-guidelines","content":"**OLED Window**: Leave an empty/transparent cutout at `(960, 32)` with dimensions `288 × 128 px` to preserve the dynamic vector oscilloscope and parameter display.","locale":"en"},"1155":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/installation","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/installation","type":"page","content":"Installation","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Getting started","Getting started"],"tags":[],"u