le":"en"},"1208":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-14","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#2-meet-the-six-rows","content":"`C` / `P` copy and paste the row's pattern.","locale":"en"},"1209":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-15","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#2-meet-the-six-rows","content":"The two knobs set the **length** (1–32 steps) and the **volume** (0–100 %).","locale":"en"},"1210":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-16","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#2-meet-the-six-rows","content":"Clicking anywhere on a row **selects** it: the synth, filter, reverb and modulation cables\nre-bind to that sequence.","locale":"en"},"1211":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-17","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#toggle-steps","content":"On row **S1**, click for instance steps 1, 5, 9 and 13.","locale":"en"},"1212":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-18","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#start-playback","content":"Click **Play** in the **CLOCK** panel. The button turns green and an orange marker\nfollows the playhead on every row.","locale":"en"},"1213":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-19","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#set-the-tempo","content":"Turn the large **CLOCK** knob (20–300 BPM, default 120).","locale":"en"},"1214":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-20","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#set-the-tempo","content":"Check in this order: (1) at least one step is active on the row, (2) **Play** is engaged,\n(3) the sequence **volume** is not at 0 %, (4) **Mix VCO1/VCO2** is not at −60 dB,\n(5) the **VCF** cutoff is not muting the signal.\nDetails: Troubleshooting.","locale":"en"},"1215":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-21","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#4-shape-the-sound","content":"The **synth** panel (bottom-left) acts on the selected sequence:","locale":"en"},"1216":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-22","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#4-shape-the-sound","content":"| Column             | Effect                                   |\n| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------- |\n| **Octave** (lever) | transposes the VCO from −2 to +2 octaves |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1217":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-23","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#4-shape-the-sound","content":"| Column                  | Effect                                             |\n| ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Note** (12 positions) | semitone from 0 (C) to 11 (B), base C3 = 130.81 Hz |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1218":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-24","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#4-shape-the-sound","content":"| Column   | Effect                         |\n| -------- | ------------------------------ |\n| **Wave** | sine / saw / square / triangle |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1219":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-25","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#4-shape-the-sound","content":"| Column   | Effect                                  |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| **ADSR** | attack, decay, sustain, release per VCO |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1220":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-26","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#4-shape-the-sound","content":"| Column         | Effect                              |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| **Mix out DB** | level of each VCO from −60 to +6 dB |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1221":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-27","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#4-shape-the-sound","content":"Bottom-centre, the **VCF** selects **LPF** or **HPF** and sets the **cutoff** (20 Hz – 20 kHz).\nOn the right: **reverb** (On/Off, Room/Hall, Mix) and the two **LFOs**.","locale":"en"},"1222":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-28","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#5-watch-the-display","content":"The OLED screen (top-right) always shows:","locale":"en"},"1223":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-29","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#5-watch-the-display","content":"the **selected sequence** number;","locale":"en"},"1224":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-30","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#5-watch-the-display","content":"the **touched parameter** and its value for 2 seconds after a change\n(e.g. `attack 120 ms`, `seq 3 volume 80 %`);","locale":"en"},"1225":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-31","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#5-watch-the-display","content":"an output **RMS bar**.","locale":"en"},"1226":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-32","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#next-step","content":"<Card title=\"The sequencer in depth\" href=\"/en/docs/guide/sequencer\" />","locale":"en"},"1227":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-33","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#next-step","content":"<Card title=\"The per-sequence synth\" href=\"/en/docs/guide/synth\" />","locale":"en"},"1228":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start-34","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start#next-step","content":"<Card title=\"LFOs and modulation cables\" href=\"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation\" />","locale":"en"},"1229":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","type":"page","content":"Melodic Arpeggiator","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","User guide","User guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","locale":"en"},"1230":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","content":"11 algorithmic modes, 10 chords & scales, up to 3-octave span, and sample-accurate step-gated triggers.","locale":"en"},"1231":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#operating-principles","content":"Operating Principles","locale":"en"},"1232":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#arpeggiator-controls","content":"Arpeggiator Controls","locale":"en"},"1233":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-11-algorithmic-modes","content":"The 11 Algorithmic Modes","locale":"en"},"1234":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-10-chords-and-scales","content":"The 10 Chords and Scales","locale":"en"},"1235":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#metric-phasing-with-polyrhythms","content":"Metric Phasing with Polyrhythms","locale":"en"},"1236":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","content":"Metulifer's **Arpeggiator** transforms rhythmic pulse sequences into evolving melodic lines.\nEach of the six sequencer lanes operates its own independent arpeggiator engine.","locale":"en"},"1237":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#operating-principles","content":"In Metulifer, the 32-step sequence grid establishes the **rhythm and gate**, while the arpeggiator calculates the **musical pitch** on each active step trigger:","locale":"en"},"1238":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#operating-principles","content":"When the arpeggiator shifts note pitch, the semitone offset is applied concurrently to both **VCO1** and **VCO2**, flawlessly preserving interval relationships (octave jumps, stacked fifths, or micro-detuning).","locale":"en"},"1239":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#arpeggiator-controls","content":"You can control the arpeggiator from two locations:","locale":"en"},"1240":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#arpeggiator-controls","content":"**On Each Sequence Row**: A dedicated **ARP** toggle button (adjacent to Copy `C` and Paste `P`) switches the effect on/off instantly.","locale":"en"},"1241":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#arpeggiator-controls","content":"**Inside SynthPanel**: A dedicated **ARP** column provides deep controls for the active sequence:","locale":"en"},"1242":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#arpeggiator-controls","content":"| Control      | Parameter          | Range | Description                      |\n| ------------ | ------------------ | ----- | -------------------------------- |\n| **On / Off** | `seqN_arp_enabled` | Bool  | Master arpeggiator enable switch |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1243":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#arpeggiator-controls","content":"| Control  | Parameter       | Range    | Description                                |\n| -------- | --------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| **Mode** | `seqN_arp_mode` | 11 modes | Stepping pattern and note order trajectory |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1244":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#arpeggiator-controls","content":"| Control   | Parameter        | Range              | Description                                          |\n| --------- | ---------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Chord** | `seqN_arp_chord` | 10 scales / chords | Harmonic interval pool (Major, Minor, Pentatonic...) |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1245":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#arpeggiator-controls","content":"| Control     | Parameter          | Range | Description                                     |\n| ----------- | ------------------ | ----- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| **Octaves** | `seqN_arp_octaves` | 1 – 3 | Expands the note pool across 1, 2, or 3 octaves |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1246":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-11-algorithmic-modes","content":"Clicking the **Mode** button cycles through 11 melodic algorithms:","locale":"en"},"1247":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-11-algorithmic-modes","content":"| Mode   | Algorithmic Trajectory                                |\n| ------ | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Up** | Ascends from root to top: `0, 1, 2, 3...` then wraps. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1248":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-11-algorithmic-modes","content":"| Mode     | Algorithmic Trajectory                         |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| **Down** | Descends from high to root: `N-1, N-2, N-3...` |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1249":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-11-algorithmic-modes","content":"| Mode        | Algorithmic Trajectory                                              |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Up&Down** | Ascends to the peak then bounces downward: `0, 1, 2, 3, 2, 1, 0...` |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1250":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-11-algorithmic-modes","content":"| Mode        | Algorithmic Trajectory                                    |\n| ----------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Down&Up** | Descends to root then bounces upward: `N-1, N-2, 0, 1...` |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1251":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-11-algorithmic-modes","content":"| Mode         | Algorithmic Trajectory                                                                  |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Pinky Up** | Alternates the root note (thumb) with climbing scale notes: `0, 1, 0, 2, 0, 3, 0, 4...` |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1252":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-11-algorithmic-modes","content":"| Mode           | Algorithmic Trajectory                                                        |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Pinky Down** | Alternates top peak note with descending scale notes: `N-1, N-2, N-1, N-3...` |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1253":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-11-algorithmic-modes","content":"| Mode            | Algorithmic Trajectory                                               |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Thumb-Pinky** | Bounces between extreme outer intervals: `0, N-1, 1, N-2, 2, N-3...` |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1254":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-11-algorithmic-modes","content":"| Mode         | Algorithmic Trajectory                                          |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Converge** | Inward movement starting from outer edges converging to center. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1255":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-11-algorithmic-modes","content":"| Mode        | Algorithmic Trajectory                                       |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Diverge** | Outward movement starting from center spreading to extremes. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1256":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-11-algorithmic-modes","content":"| Mode       | Algorithmic Trajectory                                              |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Random** | Non-repeating pseudo-random selection across the active chord pool. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1257":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-11-algorithmic-modes","content":"| Mode      | Algorithmic Trajectory                                                |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Order** | Strictly steps through notes in the natural order of scale intervals. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1258":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-11-algorithmic-modes","content":"**Pinky Up** is modeled after iconic 1980s synth-bass keyboard technique: your left thumb holds down the driving bass pedal while your pinky taps accent notes higher up the keyboard.","locale":"en"},"1259":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-10-chords-and-scales","content":"Clicking the **Chord** button selects the harmonic palette:","locale":"en"},"1260":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-10-chords-and-scales","content":"| Chord / Scale | Intervals (semitones) | Musical Mood                   |\n| ------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| **Major**     | `0, 4, 7, 12`         | Bright, triumphant major triad |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"1261":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-10-chords-and-scales","content":"| Chord / Scale | Intervals (semitones) | Musical Mood              |\n| ------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| **Minor**     | `0, 3, 7, 12`         | Dark, emotive minor triad |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"1262":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-10-chords-and-scales","content":"| Chord / Scale  | Intervals (semitones) | Musical Mood                              |\n| -------------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| **Pentatonic** | `0, 3, 5, 7, 10, 12`  | Driving, versatile minor pentatonic scale |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"1263":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-10-chords-and-scales","content":"| Chord / Scale | Intervals (semitones) | Musical Mood                     |\n| ------------- | --------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| **Octaves**   | `0, 12, 24`           | Pure octave leaps for bass stabs |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"1264":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-10-chords-and-scales","content":"| Chord / Scale | Intervals (semitones) | Musical Mood                                     |\n| ------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Maj7**      | `0, 4, 7, 11, 12`     | Dreamy, lush major 7th chords for ambient & jazz |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"1265":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-10-chords-and-scales","content":"| Chord / Scale | Intervals (semitones) | Musical Mood                          |\n| ------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| **Min7**      | `0, 3, 7, 10, 12`     | Deep house, neo-soul minor 7th warmth |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"1266":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-10-chords-and-scales","content":"| Chord / Scale | Intervals (semitones) | Musical Mood                           |\n| ------------- | --------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| **Dom7**      | `0, 4, 7, 10, 12`     | Gritty funk & blues dominant 7th color |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"1267":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-10-chords-and-scales","content":"| Chord / Scale | Intervals (semitones) | Musical Mood                            |\n| ------------- | --------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| **Sus4**      | `0, 5, 7, 12`         | Suspended 4th, modern cinematic tension |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"1268":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-10-chords-and-scales","content":"| Chord / Scale | Intervals (semitones) | Musical Mood                               |\n| ------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| **Fifths**    | `0, 7, 12, 19`        | Power chords, great with Redux bitcrushing |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"1269":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#the-10-chords-and-scales","content":"| Chord / Scale | Intervals (semitones) | Musical Mood                    |\n| ------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| **Chromatic** | `0, 1, 2, ..., 12`    | Full 12-tone chromatic spectrum |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"1270":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/arpeggiator#metric-phasing-with-polyrhythms","content":"When combining an arpeggiator pool with an uneven count (e.g., **Min7** across 2 octaves = 9 notes) with a 16-step sequence, the melody naturally shifts across measures, producing evolving non-looping lines without needing complex generative tools.","locale":"en"},"1271":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","type":"page","content":"Filter (VCF)","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","User guide","User guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/filter","locale":"en"},"1272":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/filter","content":"Low-pass or high-pass TPT filter, cutoff 20 Hz – 20 kHz, per sequence.","locale":"en"},"1273":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#two-exclusive-modes","content":"Two exclusive modes","locale":"en"},"1274":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#cutoff","content":"Cutoff","locale":"en"},"1275":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#implementation","content":"Implementation","locale":"en"},"1276":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#signal-order","content":"Signal order","locale":"en"},"1277":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#modulation-target","content":"Modulation target","locale":"en"},"1278":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#two-exclusive-modes","content":"The **VCF** panel offers two mutually exclusive buttons:","locale":"en"},"1279":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#two-exclusive-modes","content":"| Button  | Parameter `seqN_filter` | Behaviour                                     |\n| ------- | ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| **LPF** | `0`                     | low-pass: passes frequencies below the cutoff |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1280":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#two-exclusive-modes","content":"| Button  | Parameter `seqN_filter` | Behaviour                                      |\n| ------- | ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| **HPF** | `1`                     | high-pass: passes frequencies above the cutoff |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1281":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#two-exclusive-modes","content":"Clicking the already-active button does nothing: the choice is always exactly one of the two.","locale":"en"},"1282":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#cutoff","content":"| Parameter | ID            | Range                          | Default  |\n| --------- | ------------- | ------------------------------ | -------- |\n| Cutoff    | `seqN_cutoff` | 20 Hz – 20,000 Hz (skew 1 kHz) | 1,000 Hz |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1283":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#cutoff","content":"The cutoff is **skewed** around 1 kHz: the musically useful range (100 Hz – 5 kHz)\noccupies most of the knob's travel.","locale":"en"},"1284":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#cutoff","content":"The frequency is clamped in code to `min(cutoff, sampleRate × 0.49)`.\nAt 44.1 kHz the effective maximum is therefore ≈ 21.6 kHz; at 96 kHz the 20 kHz\nsetting stays unchanged.","locale":"en"},"1285":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#implementation","content":"The filter is a **State Variable TPT** (`juce::dsp::StateVariableTPTFilter<float>`),\nused in low-pass or high-pass mode:","locale":"en"},"1286":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#implementation","content":"Characteristics:","locale":"en"},"1287":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#implementation","content":"**topology-preserving variable state** (TPT / SVF) → stable response even at high cutoff;","locale":"en"},"1288":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#implementation","content":"**1 channel** processed per voice (the signal is mono before the reverb);","locale":"en"},"1289":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#implementation","content":"**no exposed resonance** for now (fixed Q);","locale":"en"},"1290":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#implementation","content":"the filter runs **after** summing both VCOs and **before** the sequence volume.","locale":"en"},"1291":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#signal-order","content":"The filter is therefore **per voice**, not global: every sequence has its own cutoff.\nSelecting another sequence in the UI re-binds the **Cutoff** knob to the new sequence.","locale":"en"},"1292":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/filter-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/filter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/filter#modulation-target","content":"`cutoff` is one of the destinations accepted by LFO cables.\nSee LFOs and modulation cables.","locale":"en"},"1293":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","type":"page","content":"Interface and display","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","User guide","User guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/interface","locale":"en"},"1294":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface","content":"Map of the 1280 × 720 UI, OLED screen, pagination and component inspector.","locale":"en"},"1295":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#ui-map","content":"UI map","locale":"en"},"1296":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#the-oled-display--studio-monitoring","content":"The OLED Display & Studio Monitoring","locale":"en"},"1297":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#1-phase-locked-real-time-oscilloscope","content":"1. Phase-Locked Real-Time Oscilloscope","locale":"en"},"1298":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#2-studio-stereo-dbfs-meter","content":"2. Studio Stereo dBFS Meter","locale":"en"},"1299":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#3-contextual-parameter-display","content":"3. Contextual Parameter Display","locale":"en"},"1300":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#clock-panel--transport-control","content":"CLOCK Panel & Transport Control","locale":"en"},"1301":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#factory-presets-bank","content":"Factory Presets Bank","locale":"en"},"1302":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#live-lfo-modulation-feedback","content":"Live LFO Modulation Feedback","locale":"en"},"1303":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#pagination-by-selection","content":"Pagination by selection","locale":"en"},"1304":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#hardware-graphics-acceleration--120-fps-fluidity","content":"Hardware Graphics Acceleration & 120 FPS Fluidity","locale":"en"},"1305":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#component-inspector","content":"Component inspector","locale":"en"},"1306":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#hardware-theme","content":"“Hardware” theme","locale":"en"},"1307":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#shortcuts-and-helpers","content":"Shortcuts and helpers","locale":"en"},"1308":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#ui-map","content":"The editor is **1280 × 720** and places its panels at absolute coordinates\n(`resized()` in `Source/PluginEditor.cpp`).","locale":"en"},"1309":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#ui-map","content":"| Panel                               | Position (x, y) | Size      |\n| ----------------------------------- | --------------- | --------- |\n| Sequencer (6 rows with ARP toggles) | 32, 32          | 910 × 417 |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1310":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#ui-map","content":"| Panel        | Position (x, y) | Size      |\n| ------------ | --------------- | --------- |\n| OLED display | 986, 32         | 247 × 132 |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1311":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#ui-map","content":"| Panel | Position (x, y) | Size      |\n| ----- | --------------- | --------- |\n| CLOCK | 961, 164        | 297 × 284 |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1312":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#ui-map","content":"| Panel                                    | Position (x, y) | Size      |\n| ---------------------------------------- | --------------- | --------- |\n| Synth (2 VCO, 2 ADSR, Mix, ARP controls) | 32, 458         | 786 × 237 |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1313":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#ui-map","content":"| Panel                | Position (x, y) | Size      |\n| -------------------- | --------------- | --------- |\n| VCF (LPF/HPF filter) | 684, 471        | 105 × 224 |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1314":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#ui-map","content":"| Panel | Position (x, y) | Size      |\n| ----- | --------------- | --------- |\n| LFO 1 | 874, 471        | 105 × 224 |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1315":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#ui-map","content":"| Panel | Position (x, y) | Size      |\n| ----- | --------------- | --------- |\n| LFO 2 | 1013, 471       | 105 × 224 |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1316":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#ui-map","content":"| Panel                          | Position (x, y) | Size      |\n| ------------------------------ | --------------- | --------- |\n| Multi-FX (Tabs: REV, DLY, RDX) | 1144, 471       | 105 × 224 |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1317":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#ui-map","content":"| Panel              | Position (x, y) | Size    |\n| ------------------ | --------------- | ------- |\n| **Inspect** button | 1188, 8         | 60 × 18 |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1318":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#ui-map","content":"The `CableLayer` covers the whole window (0, 0, 1280, 720) but its `hitTest()` only\nreturns `true` near a jack or a cable: clicks pass through everywhere else.","locale":"en"},"1319":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#the-oled-display--studio-monitoring","content":"The central display is synchronized at **60 Hz** with zero perceived latency:","locale":"en"},"1320":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#1-phase-locked-real-time-oscilloscope","content":"When parameters are untouched, the screen renders an ultra-precise oscilloscope trace:","locale":"en"},"1321":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#1-phase-locked-real-time-oscilloscope","content":"**Rising Zero-Crossing Trigger**: Automatic trigger detection locks waveform phase in place, keeping the waveform steady with zero jitter or drift.","locale":"en"},"1322":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#1-phase-locked-real-time-oscilloscope","content":"**Dynamic Period Scaling**: Measures fundamental frequency to always display exactly **2 full waveform cycles**, regardless of the pitch played.","locale":"en"},"1323":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#1-phase-locked-real-time-oscilloscope","content":"**Adaptive Auto-Gain**: Fits vertical amplitude to occupy ~82% of screen height with a soft decay to flat line during silence.","locale":"en"},"1324":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#1-phase-locked-real-time-oscilloscope","content":"**Measurement Graticule**: Subtle vector grid lines at 25%, 50%, and 75% height.","locale":"en"},"1325":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#2-studio-stereo-dbfs-meter","content":"Below the oscilloscope is a calibrated professional stereo dBFS meter:","locale":"en"},"1326":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#2-studio-stereo-dbfs-meter","content":"**Independent L and R channels**: Dual bargraphs reading from -48 dBFS to +3 dBFS.","locale":"en"},"1327":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#2-studio-stereo-dbfs-meter","content":"**Instant Attack & Logarithmic Fallback**: Zero-latency peak capture with natural 54 dB/s logarithmic decay.","locale":"en"},"1328":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#2-studio-stereo-dbfs-meter","content":"**1-Second Peak Hold**: Retains maximum transient peaks for 1 second before decaying.","locale":"en"},"1329":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#2-studio-stereo-dbfs-meter","content":"**CLIP Indicator**: High-contrast red alert when exceeding 0 dBFS.","locale":"en"},"1330":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#2-studio-stereo-dbfs-meter","content":"**Tenth-of-a-dB Readout**: Real-time numerical display (e.g. `-6.2 dB` or `-inf dB`).","locale":"en"},"1331":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#3-contextual-parameter-display","content":"Whenever a knob or button is adjusted, the screen shifts immediately into amber **EDIT** mode for 2 seconds:","locale":"en"},"1332":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#3-contextual-parameter-display","content":"Displays full parameter name, exact value, and unit (e.g. `seq 1 cutoff 1250 Hz`, `tempo 128.0 BPM`, `reverb Room`).","locale":"en"},"1333":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#3-contextual-parameter-display","content":"Shows sequencer feedback alerts (e.g. `SEQ 1 COPIED`, `SEQ 2 PASTED`).","locale":"en"},"1334":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#clock-panel--transport-control","content":"Positioned below the OLED screen, the **CLOCK** panel (961, 164) houses the master timing controls:","locale":"en"},"1335":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#clock-panel--transport-control","content":"**Tempo Rotary Knob**: Adjusts playback speed from 20.0 to 300.0 BPM.","locale":"en"},"1336":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#clock-panel--transport-control","content":"**Play/Stop Button**: Manually triggers or pauses sequencer playback in free-running mode.","locale":"en"},"1337":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#clock-panel--transport-control","content":"**Sync Toggle Button**: Engages real-time synchronization with the host Digital Audio Workstation (DAW). When active, tempo and transport tracking are slaved to the DAW timeline.","locale":"en"},"1338":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#factory-presets-bank","content":"Metulifer includes **8 curated factory presets** spanning diverse electronic styles (techno, acid, ambient, lo-fi, synthwave). These presets are natively accessible via standard DAW preset menus and support MIDI *Program Change* messages:","locale":"en"},"1339":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#factory-presets-bank","content":"| #     | Preset Name      | Sonic Character & Musical Applications                                                                  |\n| ----- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **1** | `Default / Init` | Neutral, clean initialization patch. Ideal for starting sound design and custom sequences from scratch. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1340":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#factory-presets-bank","content":"| #     | Preset Name      | Sonic Character & Musical Applications                                                                          |\n| ----- | ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **2** | `Berlin Minimal` | Hypnotic Berlin underground club techno. Punchy sub-bass, syncopated ping-pong delay, and dark minimal grooves. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1341":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#factory-presets-bank","content":"| #     | Preset Name | Sonic Character & Musical Applications                                                                   |\n| ----- | ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **3** | `Acid 303`  | Incisive, squelchy TB-303 inspired acid basslines, biting resonance, and short punchy envelope contours. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1342":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#factory-presets-bank","content":"| #     | Preset Name     | Sonic Character & Musical Applications                                                      |\n| ----- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **4** | `Ambient Glass` | Floating ethereal textures, deep cathedral hall reverb, and slow contemplative polyrhythms. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1343":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#factory-presets-bank","content":"| #     | Preset Name       | Sonic Character & Musical Applications                                                                     |\n| ----- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **5** | `Lo-Fi Nostalgia` | Warm vintage analog character, subtle texture degradation via Redux downsampling, and gentle pitch drifts. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1344":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#factory-presets-bank","content":"| #     | Preset Name         | Sonic Character & Musical Applications                                                                    |\n| ----- | ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **6** | `Industrial Crunch` | Harsh metallic percussions and digital overdrive, biting high-pass filtering, and aggressive polyrhythms. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1345":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#factory-presets-bank","content":"| #     | Preset Name    | Sonic Character & Musical Applications                                                              |\n| ----- | -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **7** | `Melodic Arps` | Shimmering melodic arpeggios voiced across fifths and octaves with open, crystalline top-end sheen. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1346":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#factory-presets-bank","content":"| #     | Preset Name       | Sonic Character & Musical Applications                                            |\n| ----- | ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **8** | `Cyberpunk Drive` | Gritty, cinematic synthwave bass, cutting transients, and fast LFO filter sweeps. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1347":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#live-lfo-modulation-feedback","content":"Metulifer features a complete real-time visual feedback loop between LFO modulators and target synth knobs:","locale":"en"},"1348":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#live-lfo-modulation-feedback","content":"**LFO OLED Mini-Screens**:","locale":"en"},"1349":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#live-lfo-modulation-feedback","content":"Each LFO slice has a backlit OLED screen displaying the exact connected parameter target (e.g. `SEQ 1 CUTOFF`, `SEQ 3 DLY TIME`) or `[ UNLINKED ]`.","locale":"en"},"1350":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#live-lfo-modulation-feedback","content":"Real-time display of active waveform (`SIN`, `SAW`, `SQR`, `TRI`) and modulation frequency in Hertz (e.g. `3.5Hz`).","locale":"en"},"1351":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#live-lfo-modulation-feedback","content":"Pulsing activity indicator and LED brightness ring next to the output jack.","locale":"en"},"1352":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#live-lfo-modulation-feedback","content":"**Real-Time Modulated Knobs**:","locale":"en"},"1353":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-59","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#live-lfo-modulation-feedback","content":"Any knob modulated by an active LFO displays a dynamic **two-tone modulation arc** (amber for LFO 1, cyan for LFO 2) indicating real-time swing.","locale":"en"},"1354":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-60","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#live-lfo-modulation-feedback","content":"The knob's needle actively rotates in sync with the LFO wave.","locale":"en"},"1355":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-61","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#live-lfo-modulation-feedback","content":"A reference indicator dot marks the user's static base setting.","locale":"en"},"1356":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-62","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#pagination-by-selection","content":"A single set of knobs serves all six sequences:","locale":"en"},"1357":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-63","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#pagination-by-selection","content":"clicking a row calls `bindSequence(index)`;","locale":"en"},"1358":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-64","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#pagination-by-selection","content":"the synth, arpeggiator, VCF and Multi-FX `SliderAttachment`s are **destroyed and recreated** on the\n`seqN_*` parameters of the chosen sequence;","locale":"en"},"1359":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-65","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#pagination-by-selection","content":"an `updatingBindings` flag prevents stale display during re-binding;","locale":"en"},"1360":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-66","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#pagination-by-selection","content":"LPF/HPF, Multi-FX On/Off, PingPong, Redux On/Off, ARP On/Off, Mode and Chord buttons are synchronised through parameter listeners,\nso they also follow **host automation**.","locale":"en"},"1361":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-67","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#pagination-by-selection","content":"These controls are **not** re-bound: each has its own permanent attachment,\ncar they belong to a specific row (or to the project for tempo).","locale":"en"},"1362":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-68","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#hardware-graphics-acceleration--120-fps-fluidity","content":"The UI incorporates advanced macOS rendering optimizations:","locale":"en"},"1363":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-69","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#hardware-graphics-acceleration--120-fps-fluidity","content":"**Native Opacity (`setOpaque(true)`)**: The root plugin editor is marked opaque to the macOS WindowServer. Window dragging, repositioning, and staging are handled via hardware GPU texture blit with zero CPU redraw overhead.","locale":"en"},"1364":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-70","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#hardware-graphics-acceleration--120-fps-fluidity","content":"**Unclipped Rendering (`setPaintingIsUnclipped`)**: The 192 step buttons and static controls bypass CoreGraphics clipping path calculations, ensuring a locked 60/120 Hz refresh rate.","locale":"en"},"1365":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-71","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#component-inspector","content":"The plugin embeds **melatonin_inspector**. Two ways to open it:","locale":"en"},"1366":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-72","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#component-inspector","content":"**⌘I** shortcut;","locale":"en"},"1367":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-73","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#component-inspector","content":"the **Inspect** button, top-right.","locale":"en"},"1368":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-74","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#component-inspector","content":"The inspector lets you:","locale":"en"},"1369":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-75","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#component-inspector","content":"select any component by clicking it;","locale":"en"},"1370":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-76","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#component-inspector","content":"edit bounds, colours and margins live;","locale":"en"},"1371":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-77","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#component-inspector","content":"browse the component tree and check `LookAndFeel`s;","locale":"en"},"1372":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-78","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#component-inspector","content":"undo changes (wired to the processor's `undoManager`).","locale":"en"},"1373":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-79","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#component-inspector","content":"The inspector is compiled into every configuration. It has no impact on DSP but remains\na debugging tool: disabling it for a public release means removing the\n`melatonin::Inspector` instance from the editor.","locale":"en"},"1374":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-80","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#hardware-theme","content":"The UI does not use the default LookAndFeel:","locale":"en"},"1375":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-81","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#hardware-theme","content":"`MetuliferLookAndFeel` draws **hardware potentiometers** (groove, value arc,\nbrushed metal body, needle) and **tactile buttons** with normal / hover / down states;","locale":"en"},"1376":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-82","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#hardware-theme","content":"the arc colour depends on the control type (amber for tempo/reverb, cyan for cutoff,\nblue for volume, violet for mix, sky for ADSR);","locale":"en"},"1377":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-83","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#hardware-theme","content":"step buttons show their number and visually group 4/4 downbeats.","locale":"en"},"1378":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-84","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#hardware-theme","content":"See UI and skinning to replace these drawings with assets.","locale":"en"},"1379":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-85","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#shortcuts-and-helpers","content":"| Action            | Interaction   |\n| ----------------- | ------------- |\n| Select a sequence | click the row |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"1380":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-86","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#shortcuts-and-helpers","content":"| Action        | Interaction      |\n| ------------- | ---------------- |\n| Toggle a step | click the square |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"1381":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-87","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#shortcuts-and-helpers","content":"| Action                     | Interaction                                 |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| Show a parameter on screen | drag a knob, mouse wheel, or click a button |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"1382":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-88","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#shortcuts-and-helpers","content":"| Action              | Interaction                  |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| Create an LFO cable | drag from the jack to a knob |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"1383":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-89","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#shortcuts-and-helpers","content":"| Action         | Interaction     |\n| -------------- | --------------- |\n| Delete a cable | click the cable |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"1384":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-90","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#shortcuts-and-helpers","content":"| Action             | Interaction |\n| ------------------ | ----------- |\n| Open the inspector | `⌘I`        |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"1385":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-91","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#shortcuts-and-helpers","content":"| Action      | Interaction                        |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| Play / stop | **Play** button in the CLOCK panel |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"1386":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/interface-92","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/interface#shortcuts-and-helpers","content":"Most buttons carry an explanatory **tooltip** (one-second hover).","locale":"en"},"1387":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","type":"page","content":"LFOs and modulation cables","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","User guide","User guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","locale":"en"},"1388":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","content":"Two LFOs (rate, shape, offset, depth) wired to synth knobs with virtual patch cables.","locale":"en"},"1389":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#two-global-lfos","content":"Two global LFOs","locale":"en"},"1390":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#auto-off","content":"Auto-off","locale":"en"},"1391":{