"locale":"en"},"1414":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#auto-off","content":"In that case its output value is forced to `0` and no parameter is touched.\nThere is no ghost modulation.","locale":"en"},"1415":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#visual-feedback--lfo-oled-display","content":"To remove all guesswork when patching modulations, each LFO features dedicated live visual feedback:","locale":"en"},"1416":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#visual-feedback--lfo-oled-display","content":"**Destination OLED Screen**:","locale":"en"},"1417":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#visual-feedback--lfo-oled-display","content":"Each LFO slice has its own backlit miniature OLED screen.","locale":"en"},"1418":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#visual-feedback--lfo-oled-display","content":"Displays the connected destination parameter in real time (e.g. `SEQ 1 CUTOFF`, `SEQ 3 DLY MIX`) or `[ UNLINKED ]` when idle.","locale":"en"},"1419":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#visual-feedback--lfo-oled-display","content":"Frequency in Hertz is dynamically updated (e.g. `SIN 2.4Hz`).","locale":"en"},"1420":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#visual-feedback--lfo-oled-display","content":"A live activity dot oscillates vertically along the screen edge tracing the waveform.","locale":"en"},"1421":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#visual-feedback--lfo-oled-display","content":"**Real-Time Modulated Knobs**:","locale":"en"},"1422":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#visual-feedback--lfo-oled-display","content":"When a knob is connected to an active LFO, its needle rotates physically in rhythm with the modulating wave.","locale":"en"},"1423":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#visual-feedback--lfo-oled-display","content":"A colored dynamic arc (amber for LFO 1, cyan for LFO 2) expands and contracts between the base setting and the instantaneous modulated value.","locale":"en"},"1424":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#visual-feedback--lfo-oled-display","content":"A white indicator dot marks the user's base value.","locale":"en"},"1425":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#pick-the-sequence","content":"Click the row of the sequence whose knob you want to modulate.","locale":"en"},"1426":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#drag-from-the-jack","content":"Click the **jack** (circle at the bottom of the LFO panel) and drag.\nA green curve follows the cursor; compatible knobs light up.","locale":"en"},"1427":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#drop-on-the-knob","content":"The cable is created and stays drawn as a bézier between jack and knob.","locale":"en"},"1428":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#delete-a-cable","content":"Click the cable: it is removed from `modTree`. The action is **undoable**\n(the processor's `undoManager`).","locale":"en"},"1429":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#delete-a-cable","content":"A destination can only receive one cable. If a cable already targets that knob,\nthe new drop is ignored — delete the old one first.","locale":"en"},"1430":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#available-destinations","content":"| Suffix                 | Parameter  | Type      |\n| ---------------------- | ---------- | --------- |\n| `a1`, `d1`, `s1`, `r1` | `seqN_a1`… | VCO1 ADSR |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1431":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#available-destinations","content":"| Suffix                 | Parameter  | Type      |\n| ---------------------- | ---------- | --------- |\n| `a2`, `d2`, `s2`, `r2` | `seqN_a2`… | VCO2 ADSR |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1432":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#available-destinations","content":"| Suffix         | Parameter                | Type       |\n| -------------- | ------------------------ | ---------- |\n| `mix1`, `mix2` | `seqN_mix1`, `seqN_mix2` | VCO levels |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1433":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#available-destinations","content":"| Suffix   | Parameter     | Type       |\n| -------- | ------------- | ---------- |\n| `cutoff` | `seqN_cutoff` | VCF filter |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1434":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#available-destinations","content":"| Suffix       | Parameter         | Type            |\n| ------------ | ----------------- | --------------- |\n| `reverb_mix` | `seqN_reverb_mix` | Multi-FX Reverb |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1435":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#available-destinations","content":"| Suffix                                      | Parameter      | Type           |\n| ------------------------------------------- | -------------- | -------------- |\n| `delay_time`, `delay_feedback`, `delay_mix` | `seqN_delay_*` | Multi-FX Delay |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1436":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#available-destinations","content":"| Suffix                                  | Parameter      | Type           |\n| --------------------------------------- | -------------- | -------------- |\n| `redux_bits`, `redux_rate`, `redux_mix` | `seqN_redux_*` | Multi-FX Redux |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1437":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#available-destinations","content":"| Suffix        | Parameter          | Type                |\n| ------------- | ------------------ | ------------------- |\n| `arp_octaves` | `seqN_arp_octaves` | Arpeggiator octaves |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1438":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#available-destinations","content":"Deliberately excluded in v1: `octave`, `note`, `wave`, `length`, `volume`, `tempo`.","locale":"en"},"1439":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#how-modulation-is-applied","content":"Modulation is applied **per audio block**, on a **copy** of the read parameters:","locale":"en"},"1440":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#how-modulation-is-applied","content":"Consequences:","locale":"en"},"1441":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#how-modulation-is-applied","content":"the **APVTS is never written** by the audio thread → no feedback to the host,\nno automation conflict;","locale":"en"},"1442":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#how-modulation-is-applied","content":"maximum amplitude is **±50 % of the parameter range**;","locale":"en"},"1443":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#how-modulation-is-applied","content":"modulation is applied **before** `voice.setParams()`, i.e. for the current block.","locale":"en"},"1444":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#visual-scope","content":"Cables are only drawn for the **selected sequence**. Switching sequences hides other\nsequences' cables without deleting them: they reappear when you come back.","locale":"en"},"1445":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#persistence","content":"Cables live in a dedicated `ValueTree`:","locale":"en"},"1446":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#persistence","content":"`modTree` is serialised with `apvts` and `stepsTree` in `getStateInformation()`.\nCables are therefore restored when the project is reloaded.","locale":"en"},"1447":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation-59","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/lfo-modulation#memory-layout","content":"The processor keeps **two cable buffers** (`cableBuffers[2][32]`) and an atomic\n`activeBuffer` index. The message thread writes into the inactive buffer then flips\nthe index: the audio thread always reads a coherent buffer, lock-free.","locale":"en"},"1448":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","type":"page","content":"Modulation Matrix (Mod Matrix)","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","User guide","User guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","locale":"en"},"1449":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","content":"Multi-source routing matrix inspired by Ableton Wavetable and Drift with bipolar depths (-100% to +100%) and LFO cross-modulation.","locale":"en"},"1450":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#overview","content":"Overview","locale":"en"},"1451":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#6-modulation-sources","content":"6 Modulation Sources","locale":"en"},"1452":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#15-synthesis--fx-destinations","content":"15 Synthesis & FX Destinations","locale":"en"},"1453":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#synthesis--filter-synth-filter","content":"Synthesis & Filter (SYNTH Filter)","locale":"en"},"1454":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#envelopes--multi-fx-fx-filter","content":"Envelopes & Multi-FX (FX Filter)","locale":"en"},"1455":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#cell-interaction--gestures","content":"Cell Interaction & Gestures","locale":"en"},"1456":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#navigation--filtering","content":"Navigation & Filtering","locale":"en"},"1457":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#real-time-lock-free-performance","content":"Real-Time Lock-Free Performance","locale":"en"},"1458":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#overview","content":"Metulifer's **Modulation Matrix** brings the fluid, comprehensive routing workflow of modern flagships like **Ableton Wavetable** and **Ableton Drift** into a modular step sequencer.","locale":"en"},"1459":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#overview","content":"While the virtual patch cables provide tactile 1-to-1 connections from LFOs to destination knobs, the Modulation Matrix provides an **interconnected multi-source grid** where any modulation source can drive multiple synthesis and effect destinations with bipolar depths and vector summation.","locale":"en"},"1460":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#overview","content":"Press `M` on your keyboard at any time to toggle the Modulation Matrix overlay on and off.","locale":"en"},"1461":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#6-modulation-sources","content":"| Source    | Signal Type            | Description                                                              |\n| --------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **LFO 1** | Bipolar (-1.0 to +1.0) | Multi-waveform LFO (Sine, Saw, Square, Tri) with rate from 0.1 to 20 Hz. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1462":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#6-modulation-sources","content":"| Source    | Signal Type            | Description                                     |\n| --------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| **LFO 2** | Bipolar (-1.0 to +1.0) | Independent secondary low-frequency oscillator. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1463":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#6-modulation-sources","content":"| Source     | Signal Type           | Description                                     |\n| ---------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| **ADSR 1** | Unipolar (0.0 to 1.0) | Primary amplifier envelope of the active voice. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1464":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#6-modulation-sources","content":"| Source     | Signal Type           | Description                               |\n| ---------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| **ADSR 2** | Unipolar (0.0 to 1.0) | Assignable secondary modulation envelope. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1465":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#6-modulation-sources","content":"| Source        | Signal Type            | Description                                                  |\n| ------------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Key/Pitch** | Bipolar (-1.0 to +1.0) | Key tracking normalized relative to middle C (MIDI note 60). |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1466":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#6-modulation-sources","content":"| Source       | Signal Type           | Description                                  |\n| ------------ | --------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| **Velocity** | Unipolar (0.0 to 1.0) | Dynamic trigger velocity of the active step. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1467":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#15-synthesis--fx-destinations","content":"The matrix gives you deep expressive control across all sound generation and processing modules:","locale":"en"},"1468":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#synthesis--filter-synth-filter","content":"**VCF Cutoff**: Resonant filter cutoff frequency (exponential sweep up to +/- 4 octaves).","locale":"en"},"1469":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#synthesis--filter-synth-filter","content":"**VCO 1 Pitch**: Continuous pitch offset for Oscillator 1 (+/- 24 semitones).","locale":"en"},"1470":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#synthesis--filter-synth-filter","content":"**VCO 2 Pitch**: Continuous pitch offset for Oscillator 2 (+/- 24 semitones).","locale":"en"},"1471":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#synthesis--filter-synth-filter","content":"**VCO 1 Wave**: Continuous waveshape morphing (Sine -> Saw -> Square -> Triangle).","locale":"en"},"1472":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#synthesis--filter-synth-filter","content":"**VCO 2 Wave**: Continuous waveshape morphing for Oscillator 2.","locale":"en"},"1473":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#synthesis--filter-synth-filter","content":"**Mix VCO 1**: Oscillator 1 balance and level (+/- 30 dB).","locale":"en"},"1474":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#synthesis--filter-synth-filter","content":"**Mix VCO 2**: Oscillator 2 balance and level (+/- 30 dB).","locale":"en"},"1475":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#envelopes--multi-fx-fx-filter","content":"**ADSR 1 Decay**: Primary envelope decay duration.","locale":"en"},"1476":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/mod-matrix#envelopes--multi-fx-fx-filter","content":"**ADSR 2 Decay**: Modulation envelope decay duration.","locale":"en"},"1477":{"id":"